# What is written of a value is kept from one promise of a body to the next. THE LYING CONTROLS: each of the three is reported
# arms: `a` was asked first behind `a < 100`; behind the join nothing holds it: what is kept is kept for a place . sibling: the same, in the other arm of a test that is no relation
# turns: `n` is declared nothing: the first walk of the loop knows it as an integer, the last as a number with halves: what hangs on the walk is asked anew
# THE RIGHT ONES: again: asked first where nothing holds it and reported there, `a` is held behind the test all the same . chain: each step rests on the one in front
# -- source: what-is-kept-of-a-value-holds-at-its-place-and-hangs-on-no-walk.ts
